course: dictionary
lesson: 866
title: Animals and new words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bilby is a noun, which is a name for a thing. Context tells you what kind of thing it is. «Bilbies are small desert marsupials with huge ears that rarely need to drink» tells you where a bilby lives, what it looks like and how it survives.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the new word. «The bilby is a desert marsupial with long rabbit-like ears that digs spiral burrows.» The words rabbit-like tell you what the ears look like, and digs spiral burrows tells you it lives underground. A burrow is a hole dug in the ground, so you can work that out from the word digs.
explain: Always check your guess by putting your meaning into the sentence. Try «a hole dug in the ground» in place of burrows. Does «digs spiral holes in the ground» still make sense? Yes, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: A bilby is a small Australian marsupial.
fact: A marsupial is an animal whose mother carries her babies in a pouch.
fact: Bilbies have long rabbit-like ears, a long pointed nose and silky blue-grey fur.
fact: Bilbies live in desert areas, dig burrows and come out at night.
fact: Foxes, cats and rabbits brought to Australia harmed bilbies, so they are endangered. At Easter, many Australian children buy chocolate «Easter bilbies» to help save them.
exercise: «The bilby is a desert marsupial with long rabbit-like ears that digs spiral burrows.» What is a bilby? | A type of chocolate sweet only | A fish that lives in rivers | Bird that sings in the trees | *A small Australian marsupial with long ears
exercise: «...that digs spiral burrows.» What is a burrow? | A pouch on a mother's tummy | A tall tree with thick branches | A pair of huge ears | *A hole dug in the ground
exercise: «Australians buy chocolate bilbies at Easter to raise money to save them.» Why do they do this? | Because bilbies sing at Easter | To feed the foxes | Because bilbies are too big to eat | *To help protect bilbies
test: What does marsupial mean? | A kind of desert plant | *An animal whose mother carries her babies in a pouch | An animal that has no ears | A bird that cannot fly
test: Where do bilbies live? | *In desert areas | High up in the tallest trees | Deep under the sea | In cold snowy mountains
exam: Which sentence best describes a bilby? | A sweet that children eat at Christmas | A large fish that swims in rivers | *A small desert marsupial with long rabbit-like ears and silky blue-grey fur | A bird that sings loudly at dawn
